BT /F1 11 Tf 15 TL 72 740 Td (Consistent Hashing Field Notes) Tj T* T* (A hash ring maps both keys and servers onto the same circle of 2^32 positions.) Tj T* (Each key belongs to the first server found clockwise from the key position.) Tj T* (When a server joins, only the keys between it and its predecessor move.) Tj T* (With N servers, adding one moves about 1/N of the keys instead of nearly all of them.) Tj T* T* (Virtual nodes give each physical server many positions on the ring.) Tj T* (In our example cluster, 160 virtual nodes per server kept the load within) Tj T* (plus or minus 8 percent of the mean across 12 servers.) Tj T* ET
